# tests of the RISC-V operations on a field narrower than a word: which ones
# select to the field loops and which to Zabha's direct instructions, and
# each field loop's expansion run step by step on a word, every row's
# arithmetic evaluated by the folder, against the plain operation on the
# field at its width
#
# no evaluator in the tree runs machine code, so the run here is a model of
# the rows the expansion writes, the reserved pair a single thread's load and
# store. it says what the steps compute, and never what a core does with them.

